[[Lore:Skuldafn|Skuldafn]] is an ancient temple complex containing a [[Lore:Word Walls|Word Wall]] located high in the [[Lore:Velothi Mountains|Velothi Mountains]] in [[Lore:Eastmarch|Eastmarch]]. It was built by the [[Lore:Dragon Cult|Dragon Cult]] as a temple to [[Lore:Alduin|Alduin]],{{ref|name=Odahviing|[[Skyrim:Odahviing|Odahviing's]] dialogue in [[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]}}{{ref|name=EGT|{{Cite Book|EGT|Skyrim}}}}{{ref|name=SkuldafnLoc|[[Skyrim:Skuldafn|Skuldafn]] location in [[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]}} and was later revered by the [[Lore:Nords|Nords]] as one of the holiest and most sacred dragonshrines.{{Ref|name=Jorunn|[[Online:Jorunn the Skald-King|''Jorunn the Skald-King'']]'s dialogue in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}}{{ref|name=ESOLoad|[[Online:Skuldafn|Skuldafn]]'s loading screen in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}}{{ref|name=KC|{{Cite Book|Kyne's Challenge: A Hunter's Companion|ns_base=Books}}}} The main significance of Skuldafn comes from the fact that the temple contains a portal to the Nordic afterlife of [[Lore:Sovngarde|Sovngarde]], which allows mortals to enter the realm without dying.{{ref|name=SoS|Events of [[ON:Songs of Sovngarde|Songs of Sovngarde]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}}{{ref|name=SovngardeQuest|Events of [[Skyrim:Sovngarde (quest)|Sovngarde]] in [[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]}} In {{Year|4E 201}}, Alduin used this portal to travel to Sovngarde and devour the souls of the dead, a privilege he jealously guards.{{ref|name=Odahviing}}{{ref|name=WEEQuest|Events of [[Skyrim:The World-Eater's Eyrie|The World-Eater's Eyrie]] in [[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]}}<noinclude>
